t: 0;\" class=\"mce_SELRES_start\">﻿</span>\nLearn it\nLive it\nPass it on…….\nIntroduction\nThe Department of English was established in 1963, concurrent with the founding of the college.\nInitially, it offered only Arts faculty courses. Science and Commerce streams were subsequently introduced between 1970 and 1974.\nIt boasts a team of experienced faculty members specializing in diverse areas of English literature and language studies.\nThe Department offers comprehensive undergraduate programs designed to foster critical thinking and analytical skills.\nAdditionally, the Department maintains comprising 300 books and journals.\nVision and Mission\nWe would like to offers students adequate communication skills to prepare them for the professional needs in the globalized scenario prevalent today.\nWe strive for academic excellence\nLearn it\n….\nLive it\n…..\nPass it on\n……\nFaculty Profile\nFaculty\nMr. Diganta Boro , MA, UGC NET\nAssistant Professor\ndiganta@dibrucollege.edu.in\nDr. Raujline Siraj Farjina Akhtar (Hod), M.A., M.Phil., Ph. D., SLET\nAssistant Professor\nraujline@dibrucollege.edu.in\nVacant\nAssistant Professor\nCourses and Syllabus\nCourses and Syllabus\nUG: All students admitted into College (all three semesters) are enrolled in Department of English as English is a compulsory subject.\nEnglish (Honors):\nCommenced from July 2022\nCurrent Batch: FYUGP 1\nst,\n3\nrd,\nand 5\nth\nSyllabus Link:\nClick To Download\nDepartmental Activities\nDepartmental Activities\nExtension & Outreach Activities 2022\nOctober 31, 2025\nExtension activities 2020-21\nOctober 31, 2025\nExtension activities 2019-20\nOctober 31, 2025\nExtension activities 2018-19\nOctober 31, 2025\nExtension activities 2017-2018\nOctober 31, 2025\nDEPARTMENTAL ACTIVITIES 2020-2021\nOctober 31, 2025\nDEPARTMENTAL ACTIVITIES 2019-2020\nOctober 31, 2025\nDEPARTMENTAL ACTIVITIES 2018-2019\nOctober 31, 2025\nDEPARTMENTAL ACTIVITIES 2017-2018\nOctober 31, 2025\nPublications\nPublications\nDR RAUJLINE SIRAJ FARJINA AKHTAR\nAssistant Professor\nJournal Articles:\nPublished a paper titled ‘The Emergence of New Woman in Mitra Phukan’s\nThe Collector’s Wife\nand Easterine Kire’s\nA Terrible Matriarchy: A Study\n’ in Abhibyakti\n,\na\nbi-annual peer-reviewed research Journal of women Cell, Assam College Teachers’ Association\n. Vol-IX, No-2, August 2024. ISSN 2450-0546.\nPublished a paper titled ‘Ecofeminist Consciousness in North East Indian English Poetry: A Study’ of Selected poems in the quarterly peer-reviewed multidisciplinary journal of Assam College Teachers’ Association. Vol XLIII, No-3, July 2024.\nPublished a paper titled ‘Contours of Ecological Consciousness in Anuradha Sharma Pujari’s Iyat Ekhan Aranya Asil: A study’ in the international, peer-reviewed and referred journal Literary Herald, ISSN-2454-3365, vol 9, pg. no-253-259, December 2023.\nEdited Book Chapters:\nEditor of the book titled PRISM: A Reflector of Knowledge published by Kaushubh Prakashn, Dibrugarh, Assam. ISBN: 978-81-962766-9-0.\nPublished a paper titled ‘Representation of the Subaltern Women in Manju Kapur’s Difficult Daughters: A Study’ in the edited anthology Manju Kapur: A Critical Study published by Pencraft International, New Delhi in 2022\nPublished a paper titled Ecocritical Perspectives in Northeast Indian English Poetry: A Reading of Easterine Kire’s Selected Poems in the edited book titled Literary Resonance published by English Study and Literary Forum, Dept. of English, Kakojan College and IQAC, Kakojan College in association with Purbayaon Publication, Panbazar, Guwahati in 2021.\nPublished a paper titled ‘Exploring the marginalized female voices of resistance: A reading of Easterine Kire’s A Terrible Matriarchy in the edited book Female Voices in literature, Editor. Dr. Rashmirekha Saikia published by Mittal Publications in 2020.\nQuick Location\nIGNOU\nUniversity Grant Commission\nGetting to NAAC\nDirectorate Of Higher Education\nGuwahati University\nDibrugarh Univ